---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import DashboardArt from '../../components/DashboardArt.astro';
import DataFlowDiagram from '../../components/DataFlowDiagram.astro';
import DaySequence from '../../components/DaySequence.astro';
import { stats, modules, stack, broke, differently, screenshots } from '../../data/internal-dashboard';
---
<Base title="Case study: the Internal Dashboard" section="ai"
  description="How Cameron Kuey took Doodle Pirates Foundation’s all-in-one Internal Dashboard from concept to production in under two weeks with Claude Code and AI coding agents: 152 reviewed PRs, 1,218 tests.">
  <article>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="page-head wide">
        <ol class="crumbs eyebrow" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><li><a href="/ai-builds">AI Builds</a></li><li>Case study</li></ol>
        <h1>An all-in-one Internal Dashboard, <em>concept to production in under two weeks.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">As product owner at Doodle Pirates Foundation, I designed and shipped one role-based platform for the whole team, built with Claude Code, Claude Design and AI coding agents, with a human reviewing every change.</p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <section style="padding-top:16px"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="case cs-hero">
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
          <div class="stats" style="margin-top:20px">
            {stats.map((s) => <div class="stat"><b>{s.value}</b><span>{s.label}</span></div>)}
          </div>
          <p>Role: product owner. Doodle Pirates Foundation · Director of Business Operations.</p>
        </div>
        <DashboardArt tag="Illustration · not a screenshot" />
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
      <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>The problem</h2></div>
      <div class="prose block-text">
        <p>Doodle Pirates Foundation is a nonprofit, and much of the team is neurodivergent. I built the dashboard partly to give each person one simple place that shows what to focus on each day.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
      <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>What it does</h2></div>
      <div class="prose block-text">
        <p>One role-based platform that unifies:</p>
        <ul class="taglist">{modules.map((m) => <li>{m}</li>)}</ul>
        <p>By my estimate, it avoids <strong>$1,000+ per employee in annual software costs</strong>.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
      <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>Ask Otis</h2></div>
      <div class="prose block-text">
        <p>Ask Otis is a Claude-powered assistant built into the dashboard. It creates and updates tasks, suggests milestones and catches duplicates. Nothing it proposes is saved until a person approves it.</p>
        <h2>Meeting-to-task pipeline</h2>
        <p>Meeting transcripts become proposed tasks. Once approved, the dashboard’s AI assigns them as each person’s daily focus. It saves about 5 hours a week.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
      <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>How it was built</h2></div>
      <div>
        <div class="prose block-text"><p>I directed AI coding agents as product owner and reviewed their work: 152 pull requests, each one reviewed, backed by 1,218 automated tests.</p></div>
        <dl class="spec">
          {stack.map(([k, v]) => <div><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>How data flows</h2></div>
        <div class="prose block-text"><p>Every request goes through Cloudflare Access sign-in to the API. The API reads and writes Airtable, saves docs to Google Docs and syncs schedules to Google Calendar. Ask Otis only suggests. A person approves before anything is saved.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:32px"><DataFlowDiagram /></div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>A day in the dashboard</h2></div>
        <div class="prose block-text"><p>How the team uses it on a normal day, from a meeting to finished work.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:40px"><DaySequence /></div>
    </div></section>

    {broke.length > 0 && (
      <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>What broke &amp; how I fixed it</h2></div>
        <ol class="numbered">{broke.map((b) => <li><b>{b.title}</b><p>{b.fix}</p></li>)}</ol>
      </div></section>
    )}
    {differently.length > 0 && (
      <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>What I’d do differently</h2></div>
        <ol class="numbered">{differently.map((d) => <li><p>{d}</p></li>)}</ol>
      </div></section>
    )}

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2>Screens</h2><p class="eyebrow">Sample data only</p></div>
      <div class="shots">
        {screenshots.map((s) => (
          <figure class="shot">
            <div class="shot-ph" role="img" aria-label={`Placeholder: ${s.label} screenshot coming soon`}>
              <span class="tag">Screenshot coming soon</span>
              <div class="shot-lines" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i style="width:60%"></i><i style="width:75%"></i></div>
            </div>
            <figcaption><b>{s.label}</b><span>{s.note}</span></figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="caption" style="margin-top:20px">The dashboard and its code belong to Doodle Pirates Foundation and are private. Screenshots will use its sample-data mode.</p>
      <div class="btns"><a class="btn solid" href="/ai-builds">More AI builds →</a><a class="btn" href="/contact">Ask me about it</a></div>
    </div></section>
  </article>
</Base>
